{
  "title": "TKA Aseptic Loosening",
  "url": "https://www.orthobullets.com/recon/12754/tka-aseptic-loosening",
  "subtitle": "Updated: Mar 8 2024",
  "sections": [
    {
      "text": "summary",
      "table": null,
      "images": [],
      "importance": "3",
      "children": [
        {
          "text": "TKA Aseptic Loosening is a macrophage-induced inflammatory response that results in bone loss and implant loosening in the absence of an infection.",
          "table": null,
          "images": [],
          "importance": "3",
          "children": []
        },
        {
          "text": "Diagnosis can be made with plain radiographs of the knee.",
          "table": null,
          "images": [],
          "importance": "5",
          "children": []
        },
        {
          "text": "Treatment is generally revision arthroplasty with exchange of all loose components.",
          "table": null,
          "images": [],
          "importance": "-1",
          "children": []
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "Etiology",
      "table": null,
      "images": [],
      "importance": "-1",
      "children": [
        {
          "text": "Steps in the process include",
          "table": null,
          "images": [],
          "importance": "3",
          "children": [
            {
              "text": "**particulate debris formation**",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "5",
              "children": []
            },
            {
              "text": "**macrophage activated osteolysis**",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "4",
              "children": []
            },
            {
              "text": "**prosthesis micromotion**",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "4",
              "children": []
            },
            {
              "text": "**particulate debris dissemination**",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "4",
              "children": []
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "Pathophysiology",
          "table": null,
          "images": [],
          "importance": "3",
          "children": [
            {
              "text": "factors affecting wear rate of polyethylene in TKA",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "3",
              "children": [
                {
                  "text": "**sterilization method**",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "4",
                  "children": []
                },
                {
                  "text": "manufacturing method (conventional vs. crosslinked)",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "3",
                  "children": []
                },
                {
                  "text": "presence of third-body debris",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "3",
                  "children": []
                },
                {
                  "text": "motion between modular tibial insert and metal tray (i.e., backside wear)",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "3",
                  "children": []
                },
                {
                  "text": "roughness of femoral component counterface",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "3",
                  "children": []
                },
                {
                  "text": "**alignment and stability of the TKA**",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "4",
                  "children": [
                    {
                      "text": "malalignment causes asymmetric loading causes early loosening",
                      "table": null,
                      "images": [],
                      "importance": "4",
                      "children": []
                    },
                    {
                      "text": "more frequent with varus rather than valgus malalignment",
                      "table": null,
                      "images": [],
                      "importance": "4",
                      "children": []
                    }
                  ]
                },
                {
                  "text": "demand or **activity level of patient**",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "4",
                  "children": []
                }
              ]
            },
            {
              "text": "Aseptic loosening can also occur due to disruption of the cement-implant or cement-bone interface",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "-1",
              "children": [
                {
                  "text": "implant-cement interface is most common \"weak link\" compared to bone-cement interface",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "-1",
                  "children": []
                },
                {
                  "text": "can be avoided by minimizing lipid contamination at cement interfaces and allowing cement to fully cure before stress testing",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "-1",
                  "children": []
                }
              ]
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "Presentation",
      "table": null,
      "images": [],
      "importance": "3",
      "children": [
        {
          "text": "Symptoms",
          "table": null,
          "images": [],
          "importance": "3",
          "children": [
            {
              "text": "painless",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "3",
              "children": [
                {
                  "text": "early disease",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "3",
                  "children": []
                }
              ]
            },
            {
              "text": "pain",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "3",
              "children": [
                {
                  "text": "location",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "3",
                  "children": [
                    {
                      "text": "localized to the tissues around the loose components",
                      "table": null,
                      "images": [],
                      "importance": "3",
                      "children": []
                    }
                  ]
                },
                {
                  "text": "aggrevating factors",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "3",
                  "children": [
                    {
                      "text": "weightbearing",
                      "table": null,
                      "images": [],
                      "importance": "3",
                      "children": []
                    },
                    {
                      "text": "often activity related",
                      "table": null,
                      "images": [],
                      "importance": "3",
                      "children": []
                    }
                  ]
                }
              ]
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "Physical exam",
          "table": null,
          "images": [],
          "importance": "3",
          "children": [
            {
              "text": "may have minimal pain with ROM",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "3",
              "children": []
            },
            {
              "text": "increased pain with weight bearing",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "3",
              "children": []
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "Radiographs",
          "table": null,
          "images": [],
          "importance": "3",
          "children": [
            {
              "text": "recommended views",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "3",
              "children": [
                {
                  "text": "AP",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "3",
                  "children": [
                    {
                      "text": "tibial osteolysis readily visible on AP",
                      "table": null,
                      "images": [],
                      "importance": "3",
                      "children": []
                    },
                    {
                      "text": "**femoral osteolysis may be difficult to detect on AP** as lesions are typically located in posterior condyles and are obscured by the femoral component",
                      "table": null,
                      "images": [],
                      "importance": "4",
                      "children": []
                    }
                  ]
                },
                {
                  "text": "lateral",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "3",
                  "children": []
                },
                {
                  "text": "oblique",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "3",
                  "children": [
                    {
                      "text": "often more helpful for identifying femoral osteolysis",
                      "table": null,
                      "images": [],
                      "importance": "3",
                      "children": []
                    }
                  ]
                }
              ]
            },
            {
              "text": "findings",
              "table": null,
              "images": [
                {
                  "src": "https://upload.orthobullets.com/topic/12754/images/apos.jpg",
                  "caption": ""
                },
                {
                  "src": "https://upload.orthobullets.com/topic/12754/images/latos.jpg",
                  "caption": ""
                }
              ],
              "importance": "4",
              "children": [
                {
                  "text": "radiolucent area around implant or cement with sclerotic border",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "4",
                  "children": [
                    {
                      "text": "especially radiolucencies > 2 mm",
                      "table": null,
                      "images": [],
                      "importance": "1",
                      "children": []
                    }
                  ]
                },
                {
                  "text": "change in position of the implant",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "4",
                  "children": [
                    {
                      "text": "varus or valgus subsidence of tibial component",
                      "table": null,
                      "images": [],
                      "importance": "1",
                      "children": []
                    }
                  ]
                },
                {
                  "text": "progressive widening of cement-bone or bone-prosthesis interface",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "1",
                  "children": []
                },
                {
                  "text": "cement cracking or fragmentation",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "1",
                  "children": []
                }
              ]
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "CT Scan & MRI",
          "table": null,
          "images": [],
          "importance": "3",
          "children": [
            {
              "text": "viable options for assessing larger osteolytic lesions to aid in preoperative planning",
              "table": null,
              "images": [
                {
                  "src": "https://upload.orthobullets.com/topic/12754/images/combo.jpg",
                  "caption": ""
                }
              ],
              "importance": "1",
              "children": []
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "Studies",
      "table": null,
      "images": [],
      "importance": "3",
      "children": [
        {
          "text": "Serum labs",
          "table": null,
          "images": [],
          "importance": "3",
          "children": [
            {
              "text": "ESR normal",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "3",
              "children": []
            },
            {
              "text": "CRP normal",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "3",
              "children": []
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "Differential",
      "table": null,
      "images": [],
      "importance": "3",
      "children": [
        {
          "text": "Critical to rule out periprosthetic joint infection",
          "table": null,
          "images": [],
          "importance": "3",
          "children": []
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "Treatment",
      "table": null,
      "images": [],
      "importance": "3",
      "children": [
        {
          "text": "Nonoperative",
          "table": null,
          "images": [],
          "importance": "3",
          "children": [
            {
              "text": "observation",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "4",
              "children": [
                {
                  "text": "indications",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "1",
                  "children": [
                    {
                      "text": "stable implant with minimal symptoms",
                      "table": null,
                      "images": [],
                      "importance": "1",
                      "children": []
                    }
                  ]
                }
              ]
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "Operative",
          "table": null,
          "images": [],
          "importance": "3",
          "children": [
            {
              "text": "revision TKA",
              "table": null,
              "images": [
                {
                  "src": "https://upload.orthobullets.com/topic/12754/images/rev.jpg",
                  "caption": ""
                }
              ],
              "importance": "5",
              "children": [
                {
                  "text": "indications",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "5",
                  "children": [
                    {
                      "text": "pain due to aseptic loosening",
                      "table": null,
                      "images": [],
                      "importance": "5",
                      "children": []
                    },
                    {
                      "text": "pain with evidence of osteolysis",
                      "table": null,
                      "images": [
                        {
                          "src": "https://upload.orthobullets.com/topic/12754/images/intraop.jpg",
                          "caption": ""
                        }
                      ],
                      "importance": "5",
                      "children": []
                    },
                    {
                      "text": "extensive osteolysis that would compromise revision surgery in the future",
                      "table": null,
                      "images": [],
                      "importance": "5",
                      "children": []
                    }
                  ]
                },
                {
                  "text": "technique",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "4",
                  "children": [
                    {
                      "text": "bone graft",
                      "table": null,
                      "images": [],
                      "importance": "1",
                      "children": [
                        {
                          "text": "indicated for defects > 10 mm",
                          "table": null,
                          "images": [],
                          "importance": "1",
                          "children": []
                        },
                        {
                          "text": "often used in younger patients to preserve bone stock",
                          "table": null,
                          "images": [],
                          "importance": "1",
                          "children": []
                        }
                      ]
                    },
                    {
                      "text": "prosthetic metal wedges/augments",
                      "table": null,
                      "images": [],
                      "importance": "1",
                      "children": [
                        {
                          "text": "indicated for defects > 10 mm",
                          "table": null,
                          "images": [],
                          "importance": "1",
                          "children": []
                        },
                        {
                          "text": "often used in elderly, low activity patients",
                          "table": null,
                          "images": [],
                          "importance": "1",
                          "children": []
                        }
                      ]
                    },
                    {
                      "text": "bone cement",
                      "table": null,
                      "images": [],
                      "importance": "1",
                      "children": [
                        {
                          "text": "indicated for smaller defects",
                          "table": null,
                          "images": [],
                          "importance": "1",
                          "children": []
                        },
                        {
                          "text": "heat released can cause thermal necrosis of surrounding bone and vascular tissue which can potential lead to aseptic loosening",
                          "table": null,
                          "images": [],
                          "importance": "1",
                          "children": []
                        }
                      ]
                    }
                  ]
                }
              ]
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "Techniques",
      "table": null,
      "images": [],
      "importance": "3",
      "children": [
        {
          "text": "**Revision TKA**",
          "table": null,
          "images": [],
          "importance": "5",
          "children": []
        }
      ]
    }
